    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The Karakoram, or Karakorum is a large mountain range spanning the borders of Pakistan, India, and China, with the northwest extremity of the range extending to Afghanistan and Tajikistan. It is located in the regions of Gilgit–Baltistan (Pakistan), Ladakh (India), and southern Xinjiang (China), and reaches the Wakhan Corridor (Afghanistan). A part of the complex of ranges from the Hindu Kush to the Himalayan Range, it is one of the Greater Ranges of Asia. The Karakoram is home to the four most closely located peaks over 8000m in height on earth: K2, the second highest peak in the world at 8611 m , Gasherbrum I, Broad Peak and Gasherbrum II.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.5349286673636404,
      "temperature": 0.5349286673636404,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
